0000                                    1 ;;
0000                                    2 ; Step 3 - Generation of scroller code from a pregenerated buffer of textures
0000                                    3 ;
0000                                    4 ; Krusty/Benediction
0000                                    5 ; May 2026
0000                                    6 ;
0000                                    7 ; The main idea is as follow:
0000                                    8 ; For a given split raster line we need to generate the display code from the split raster code of the scroller. To do so we use a ring buffer that is fed with the scroll text (here we do not try to feed it is is manually done) and read to generate the soruce code for the split raster.
0000                                    9 ; However the source code is build in a kind of destructive way at the beginning and end of a line to be sure we always scroll left of 4 nops and use 64 nops of timing
0000                                   10 ;  - out (c), e activate a split raster/border pixel
0000                                   11 ;  - out (c), d deactivate a split raster/border pixel
0000                                   12 ; By convention a letter MUST end with a space
0000                                   13 ; IDEA: by also using a ring buffer for the scroller routines, we could allow a horizontal translation of the text
0000                                   14 ; IDEA it is probably possible to have a zooming scroller too by generating zoomed version of the splits
0000                                   15 ;
0008 ????? SCROLLER_NB_VERTICAL_BLOCS  16 SCROLLER_NB_VERTICAL_BLOCS equ 8
